From 26293ccaa3b321e260418f7f0418817497914db8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:14:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] joan-common: Add the AOSP IMS stack

VoLTE and Wi-Fi calling through AOSP's IMS stack. The V30's modem was
built without Qualcomm's IMS core, so IMS has to run on the AP: SIP,
IPsec and call media in ImsStack and ImsMedia, the Wi-Fi calling tunnel
in IWLAN, and the choice between LTE and Wi-Fi in QNS.

ImsStack is not in Android 15. It and ImsMedia come from Android 17
(android-17.0.0_r1) with the backport patches from
https://github.com/ShapeShifter499/joan-volte-lineage (aosp-ims/),
synced by the local manifest in that repository's upstream/aosp-ims/.
IWLAN and QNS are the tree's own.

- Build ImsStack, ImsMediaService, Iwlan and QualifiedNetworksService,
  and declare android.hardware.telephony.ims.
- Make ImsStack the device's MMTEL ImsService, allow VoLTE and Wi-Fi
  calling on the device, and bind AOSP IWLAN and QNS in place of
  vendor.qti.iwlan, which needs the modem IMS this modem does not have.
- Carrier config: VoLTE for every carrier; Wi-Fi calling for the
  carriers LG's own firmware shipped it on, matched by carrier id and
  PLMN, with the ePDG address for the US carriers that do not use the
  3GPP default name. Generated by aosp-ims/tools/make-carrier-config.py.
- Default runtime permissions: microphone and camera for ImsMedia,
  phone state and location for ImsStack, IWLAN and QNS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SByt7CZfKR6U4r1VS86tHS
